# Line endings.
#
# This repo grew a mix. index.html, tour.js, folio.js, book-utils.js,
# styles.css, folio.css, tour.css, eslint.config.js, vitest.config.js and
# tests/setup.js were stored with CRLF; everything else used LF. Nothing
# depends on that split, but it set a trap: any tool that rewrites a file
# whole (a codemod, a formatter, a quick script) silently flips its
# endings, and the commit then shows every line as changed with the real
# edit buried somewhere inside. That happened twice in a single session.
#
# text=auto tells git to store text files as LF in the repository no
# matter what the working copy uses, so a rewrite that changes endings is
# simply not a diff any more. Windows checkouts still get CRLF locally if
# core.autocrlf is set; nothing about editing on Windows changes.
#
# The commit that introduced this renormalized those ten files in one go.
# It is listed in .git-blame-ignore-revs so `git blame` and GitHub's blame
# view skip straight past it to the real authorship.
* text=auto

# Binary assets. text=auto already sniffs these correctly, but saying so
# explicitly means a new contributor's misconfigured client cannot corrupt
# a cover image or a font by "fixing" its line endings.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.pdf   binary
